From 09f2c5ae3715fc953f8b9b6091e4aa1c41868e8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:49:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0242: route the FrameHeap arena-grow overflow to the ExpHeap
 via array[0] of the global heap list (replace getCurrentHeap)

0241 used sead::getCurrentHeap (0x9564a0), but the V1.3.64 device run
proved it returns the FrameHeap during SARC loading (log-cc02472d.txt,
Football full costume: clean arena abort, backtrace byte-identical to
V1.3.62 except frame 4 = main+0x14d4264, the return after the 0241
trampoline's fail-path blr -- the guard fired and V aborted). 0240 was
wrong before it (it read [x25], struct S's first field = DATA, as a
vtable and jumped to 0x11019a0e8; DmIOS-2026-11-24-154754.ips, V1.3.63).

The new lookup reads the ExpHeap as array[0] of the global heap list at
GOT 0x13663e0 (count at +0, array at +8) -- the first heap registered,
i.e. the root ExpHeap. The game itself reads array[0] as a heap (0x942da0
passes it to the allocation helper 0x951150 and to 0x96a0c0; 0x9436d0
allocates the game's main heap FROM array[0] via vtable+0x80 and
setCurrentHeap()s the result), and array[0] is NOT the FrameHeap
(0x951150 calls [heap_vtable + 0x80] as a function, but the FrameHeap
vtable 0xdbdf00 has a DATA pointer at +0x80, 0x1352b18). The guard
compares array[0]'s vtable against 0xdbdf00 directly; on failure (empty
list, NULL array[0], FrameHeap vtable, or allocate returns 0) it calls V
directly (aborts, as before). The cut (0x954484) and the success target
(0x95448c) are unchanged. Mock 6 lines pass, asm all-pass (24-instruction
trampoline verified word for word).
